TITLE:: RETake
summary:: Take paths and the record-a-replay session
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/RERecorder, Classes/REReplay

DESCRIPTION::
Two class methods: the stamped path of a take, and the session that records a replay (an AmbiX conversion of an earlier take).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: path
argument:: root
argument:: subfolder
argument:: name
argument:: version
argument:: format
argument:: stamp
Defaults to code::Date.localtime.stamp::.
returns:: code::<root>/<subfolder>/<stamp>_<name>[ <version>].<format>::

METHOD:: session
argument:: recorder
An link::Classes/RERecorder::, prepared.
argument:: replay
An link::Classes/REReplay::, prepared, or nil.
argument:: minutes
argument:: seconds
argument:: quant
argument:: clock
Defaults to the recorder's clock.
argument:: margin
Seconds added to the duration.
returns:: The total seconds. Both start at code::quant::, the recorder stops after the total (armed at the quantized start).

EXAMPLES::

code::
RETake.session(~song.recorder(\ambix), ~song.replay(\take), minutes: 9, seconds: 24, quant: [4, 0]);
::
